ready: 1
kind: quality
id: retention.quality.deletion
display_id: QC-RETENTION-DELETION
module: retention
title: Deletion leaves nothing in Kernle's files
applies_to:
  - retention.seq.purge
  - retention.seq.stack-delete
  - retention.rule.purge-scope
measure: >-
  Presence of a purged memory's text, or a deleted capture's or event's content,
  in any file under the Kernle home after the deleting call returns, and
  whether a cloud deletion is queued for synced content
target: >-
  None present. Databases use secure delete, the full-text index is optimized,
  the write-ahead log is truncated and files are removed; a deletion change is
  queued for every purged memory that was ever synced. Filesystem recovery of
  removed blocks and the runtimes' own transcripts are outside Kernle's files.
